  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No light motif on the prayer here (it is blamed: «كسالى»). Coins for «أنفقوا» and «أموالهم»; 55 under a night sky. No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. STAGING v4: c1 (53-54): a town by day, three men (the hypocrites). Their spending is blamed and rejected, so nobody gives and there is no give gesture: a coins plate draws on 53:2 and undraws on 53:7 (not accepted); they turn their backs on 53:12 (both tafsirs: out of obedience), face again on 54:13 (coming), sit down heavily on 54:17 (lazy: As-Sa'di, heavy, they barely do it) and shake their heads on 54:22 (unwilling), under a second coins plate on 54:19 that undraws at the end. No prayer is acted for them and no light plate is on their prayer (it is blamed). c2 (55): a market by day; the same three men; a coins plate on their wealth (55:3, gone before the Name); their children are not drawn. On 55:9-10 they hurry to the middle and back (both tafsirs: the toil of gaining it); a falling-leaf plate on 55:14 (the passing away) while they stand still: nobody leaves or fades on that word. The Prophet, who is addressed, is not drawn; the camera holds on them."
 },
